notes.body:
You're looping on a lot of guint8s. For example, line 1808 has:

```
            guint8 dataset_count, idx;
            guint16 dataset_len;

            dataset_count = tvb_get_guint8(tvb, offset);
            proto_tree_add_item(zbncp_hl_body_tree, hf_zbncp_data_nvram_dataset_quantity, tvb, offset, 1, ENC_NA);
            offset += 1;

            /* multiple datasets */
            for (idx = 0; idx < dataset_count; idx++)
```

Although idx won't overflow in its current state, it's an easy thing to miss when extending the code in the future and could potentially introduce large or infinite loops. Can you make sure your loop counters are guints or even plain old ints?

